/category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/27/multimedia/27xp-phone-wipe-wkvp/27xp-phone-wipe-wkvp-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Annegret Hilse/Reuters</media:credit><media:description>A U.S. citizen used an open-source operating system, GrapheneOS, on his Google Pixel phone to “delete the digital contents,” before the device was seized, an indictment against the man said.</media:description></media:content></item></channel></rss>